sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor R as Requester
    participant UI as Streamlit app
    participant C as Amazon Cognito
    participant RT as AgentCore Runtime<br/>(Procurement Agent)
    participant G as Bedrock Guardrails
    participant LLM as Amazon Nova Lite
    participant GW as AgentCore Gateway<br/>(Policy + interceptor)
    participant T as Tool Lambdas
    participant DB as DynamoDB
    participant O as AgentCore Observability
    actor A as Approver
    participant API as Approval API<br/>(API Gateway + Lambda)
    participant S3 as S3 purchase-orders

    R->>UI: Sign in
    UI->>C: Authenticate
    C-->>UI: JWT (group = requester)
    R->>UI: "To build our test stand we need 100 pressure sensors,<br/>6 flow meters and 200 proximity sensors by Jan 30"
    UI->>RT: POST /invocations + JWT
    RT->>O: Start trace
    RT->>G: Check input (prompt attack, denied topics)
    RT->>LLM: Converse, forced extract_request tool
    LLM-->>RT: 3 items: product, quantity, specs, budget, one date
    RT->>RT: Validate, convert units, split merged specs
    RT-->>UI: Products and specs to confirm
    R->>UI: Confirm or edit each product
    UI->>RT: POST /invocations (confirmed products)
    RT->>LLM: Converse with Gateway tool list
    LLM-->>RT: get_supplier_quotes and compare_quotes for each line
    loop For each product line
        RT->>GW: MCP tools/call (line n) + OAuth token
        GW->>GW: Policy check (Cedar, default deny) and rate limit
        GW->>T: get_supplier_quotes(confirmed line n)
        T->>DB: Read SupplierCatalog for the category
        T->>T: Spec checks, volume price, stock, MOQ, budget
        T-->>RT: Best qualifying model per supplier + rejected models with reasons
        RT->>GW: compare_quotes(line n)
        GW->>T: Rank: deadline first, then 60% price / 40% delivery
        T-->>RT: Ranking and recommended supplier
    end
    RT->>RT: Group lines by winning supplier
    RT->>LLM: Tool results
    LLM-->>RT: Summary for the approver
    RT->>G: Check output (PII, grounding)
    RT->>O: End trace (latency, tokens, tool calls)
    RT-->>UI: Plan: 2 approval requests, 2 purchase orders
    R->>UI: Submit (one click)
    UI->>API: POST /orders + requester JWT
    API->>DB: Save 1 approval request per supplier (shared order id)

    Note over RT,API: The agent has no tool or route to the Approval API.

    A->>UI: Sign in (group = approver), alerted per request
    loop For each supplier request (WIKA, DwyerOmega)
        UI->>API: POST /requests/{id}/decision + approver JWT
        API->>API: Approver group, no self-approval, quotes valid,<br/>one supplier for every product, one decision only
        API->>DB: Save decision, audit event
        API->>S3: Write 1 PDF purchase order with all its products
        API-->>UI: PO number + presigned download URL
    end
    UI-->>A: 2 purchase orders, one per supplier
